From: Noxwell <beebono@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gcc-sm6125: use retention for the USB power domain

The USB subsystem does not expect to lose its state on suspend: with the
GDSC collapsing, dwc3 fails to re-enable ep0 on resume and the gadget
stays detached. Same fix as gcc-sm6115 (0008), based on upstream
25bc96f26cd6 ("clk: qcom: gcc-sc8180x: Use retention for USB power
domains").
---
diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm6125.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm6125.c
index 14ab552..9e3ac22 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm6125.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm6125.c
@@ -3766,7 +3766,7 @@ static struct gdsc usb30_prim_gdsc = {
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "usb30_prim_gdsc",
 	},
-	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
+	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_RET_ON,
 };
 
 static struct gdsc ufs_phy_gdsc = {
